   \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n\n  <p>I drew this last night while lying on the floor. it is a map of my month. in january there was: chinese mother bread + avocado toast for breakfast, a <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/dreaming-of-a-cocoon\" target=\"_blank\">caterpillar</a> who died, many dark holes I tried to avoid, three extra terrible days marked in blood, walking through <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/where-is-my-submarine\" target=\"_blank\">forest trails</a> everyday, a dear friend who visited, making <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/money-juice-cleanse\" target=\"_blank\">money juice</a> cleanse, and, long, blue shadows on sun-lit snow.<br /><br />I have been inspired by calendars as creative form. and even more so — by surrealist calendars that play with the elastic experience of time. <br /><br />*<br /><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/visual-art\" target=\"_blank\">more visual work</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"4c656157c8b017fa62ccf51b4c985405e746aa963efd1f7119564a869eb3d943","category":"Sites"}